  "releaseNotes": "v3.240.64:\n\t\t- Added: UptimeResourceOverviewReport, for LogicMonitor's Uptime Resource Overview reports.\n\t\t  ReportConverter did not model the type, so GetAllAsync<ReportBase>() threw on any portal\n\t\t  containing one, taking every other report with it - on one live portal all 241 reports were\n\t\t  unreachable because of 2. The wire format was captured rather than inferred: the\n\t\t  type-specific fields are identical to WebsiteOverviewReport, so the new class derives from\n\t\t  DateRangeReport and carries the same six properties. It is a sibling of WebsiteOverviewReport\n\t\t  rather than a subclass, because it reports on resources rather than websites.\n\t\t- Changed: ReportBase.Type's acceptable-values documentation now lists Uptime Resource\n\t\t  Overview, which it had never mentioned.\n\t\t- Unchanged, and deliberately so: an unrecognised report type still throws. Returning a base\n\t\t  instance would silently drop every type-specific field, which is a quiet wrong answer rather\n\t\t  than a graceful degrade. This client's job is to say truthfully that it does not model a\n\t\t  type; whether that is fatal is the caller's policy. A test now locks that behaviour down for\n\t\t  reports rather than leaving it merely intended.",
